2213,"n":"8BitBoy 2014","t":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2032213/movie.293x165.jpg?t=1447361737","hls":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/296910/20487/81823fddc920111aac7a86a60d728ddebcc7030d/1751262951/hls_264_master.m3u8?t=1447361737","mp4":"https://cdn.akamai.steamstatic.com/steam/apps/2032213/movie480.mp4"}],"genres":["Action","Casual","Indie"],"features":["Single-player","Family Sharing"],"platforms":{"windows":true,"mac":true,"linux":false},"controller":"full","dev":["AwesomeBlade"],"pub":["AwesomeBlade"],"released":"May 5, 2014","meta":null,"langs":["English"],"min":[["OS","Windows XP, Windows 7, Windows 8"],["Processor","Dual Core AMD or Intel / AMD E-350 APU"],["Memory","1 GB RAM"],["Graphics","Intel HD 4000 / Radeon HD 6310"],["DirectX","Version 9.0c"],["Storage","100 MB available space"],["Additional Notes","Xbox 360 controller or Keyboard"]],"rec":[],"deck":2,"blurb":"Out of work and feeling low, the title character remembers the 8-bit console of his childhood and the games he loved on it. The result is a tribute to the platformers of the 1980s and 1990s, built around classic running and jumping, power-ups, coin collecting and boss battles.\n\nThe game has 56 levels across five worlds, hidden warp zones and more than 300 secret locations to find. The main story runs roughly 8 to 12 hours. It is single-player with full controller support, suited to platformer fans who like old-school design and hunting for secrets."}}